WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.700
Before satellites, every ship crossed every ocean on one idea.

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:10.625
If I know where I started, which way I went, how fast, and for how long, I know where I am.

3
00:00:10.875 --> 00:00:17.400
That’s dead reckoning, and it’s still on the exam, and it’s still what gets you home when the screen goes dark.

4
00:00:17.650 --> 00:00:19.550
First, the symbols.

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.625
Look at the diagram.

6
00:00:21.875 --> 00:00:26.600
A fix, from two or more good lines of position, is a small circle.

7
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:32.600
A dead reckoning position, from course and speed alone, is a half circle on the course line.

8
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:39.100
An estimated position, which is a DR improved with other information, is a small square.

9
00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:43.800
And an electronic fix, from GPS, is often a triangle.

10
00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:46.575
Write the time beside every one.

11
00:00:47.575 --> 00:00:51.300
So which do you trust more: the circle, or the half circle?

12
00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.075
The circle.

13
00:00:53.325 --> 00:00:55.175
A fix is measured.

14
00:00:55.425 --> 00:00:57.575
A DR is calculated.
